names the reference product only.

runtime-libraries.tar.gz supplies the unmodified Ubuntu 24.04 shared libraries
needed by the reference installation that are absent from the agent image. It also
contains their associated data and copyright/license notices. LIBRARIES.json
lists every included file and checksum, the exact Ubuntu binary and source
package versions, and the corresponding source-package pages. Obtain those
source packages from the linked Ubuntu source publications (including the
original upstream archive and Debian/Ubuntu patch archive). With Ubuntu noble
deb-src repositories enabled, `apt-get source SOURCE_PACKAGE=SOURCE_VERSION`
retrieves that exact corresponding source. This library bundle is part of the
reference installation only; it is not installed in the agent image.

Component notices are collected in LICENSES/. Upstream copyright and license text are retained; local launch and isolation scripts are described above. The official release archive is fetched and checksum-verified at build time; SOURCE.json records its exact URL and version.

exec_guard.c is a local launcher component. Its seccomp filter is loaded with the application and denies subsequent program execution, including external commands configured in preferences. The upstream executable remains unchanged.
